Excuse.; Excusare.
Excuse.; Excusatio.

@AC 216. To "sew the leaf together" = to excuse.

@845. The ignorance and simplicity excuses; because there may be innocence in them.

@976. That those who are in internal worship and in external worship thence, interpret such things into good, and excuse. Treated of. @1085. @1087.

