@NJHD 121[2]. They who make faith alone saving, excuse a life of evil. References.

@DLW 350[3]. Ignorance does indeed excuse; but it does not take away confirmed falsity...

@CL 288. That (marriage semblances) are for the sake of excuses of blemishes.

@292[3]. I have heard excuses made by these women...

@530. There are various circumstances... which mitigate and excuse crimes...

@SE 1705. They in whom good reigns... excuse.

@2320[end]. Unless ignorance excused, it would be all over with man.

