Excuse.; Ignoscere.

@AC 986[3]. (Evil Spirits) are excused when they do evil, when they are in any use.

@1695. See <Evil Spirit>.

@2156[end]. They say that they acknowledge one Supreme Being... which is excused with those who are outside the Church.

@2203[end]. As rational truth is of such a character, it is excused, and is allowed to be in appearances...

@7250[end]. This is excused with them, because it is said from despair.

