@1062[end]. See <Japheth>.

@1080. External bonds. (See <Bind-Vincire>.)

@1173. Under <Nimrod>, see this reference.

@1680[end]. These are the externals which are removed in the other life.

@1799. That there would he only an external in the Lord's Kingdom. Signified.

@--[3]. What is doctrinal itself does not make the external (of the Church)... but it is life according to doctrinal things.

@1801. That there should not be an external of the Church. Signified.

@1802. That the external should not be the heir of His kingdom. Signified. The external is indeed the heir, but only through the internal, because they then act as one. (Explained.)

@1805. From externals sees internals. @1807.

@1815. From the mother he receives all that is external. @2005. @3128.

